https://openvtc.org/contexts/bootstrap-v1`. Maintainers verifying the proof MAY refuse other shapes."},"type":{"type":"array","minItems":2,"items":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"description":"VP types. MUST contain both `VerifiablePresentation` and `BootstrapRequest`. Additional task-specific types MAY be present."},"id":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"URN-shaped identifier for this presentation. `urn:uuid:<v4>` is RECOMMENDED."},"holder":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"pattern":"^did:key:z[1-9A-HJ-NP-Za-km-z]+\$","description":"The integration\'s ephemeral did:key (Ed25519). Identifies the party the returned bundle is HPKE-sealed for; the VP proof verifies under this DID\'s verification method."},"nonce":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{22}\$","description":"16 random bytes encoded as base64url-no-pad (22 characters). The maintainer treats this as the sealed bundle\'s `bundleId` (decoded to hex, exposed in `summary.bundleIdHex`) and SHOULD enforce one-shot semantics — a second provisioning with the same nonce MUST be refused as a replay."},"validUntil":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"Freshness bound for the VP. RFC 3339 UTC. Maintainers SHOULD allow ±5 minutes of clock skew."},"label":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":256,"description":"Optional human-readable label carried into the maintainer\'s audit log."},"ask":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/BootstrapAsk","description":"What the holder is asking the maintainer to do. Tagged on `type`; see `TemplateBootstrapAsk` and `AdminRotationAsk`."},"proof":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/DataIntegrityProof","description":"Data Integrity proof signed by the holder\'s Ed25519 key. Cryptosuite MUST equal `eddsa-jcs-2022`. `proofPurpose` MUST equal `authentication`. `verificationMethod` MUST resolve under `holder`. Signs the JCS canonicalisation of the VP with `proof` removed."}}},"BootstrapAsk":{"\$anchor":"bootstrap-ask","title":"BootstrapAsk","description":"Discriminated union of bootstrap intents. Extensible — future minor versions MAY add variants.","oneOf":[{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/TemplateBootstrapAsk"},{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/AdminRotationAsk"}]},"TemplateBootstrapAsk":{"\$anchor":"template-bootstrap-ask","title":"TemplateBootstrapAsk","description":"Mint an integration DID from `template`, and (when `adminTemplate` is present) atomically roll over the holder to a fresh long-term admin DID minted from `adminTemplate`.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["type","template"],"properties":{"type":{"const":"templateBootstrap"},"contextHint":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"Hint for the integration\'s target context. The wire `payload.context` is authoritative; this hint exists for documentation / cross-check only."},"template":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/DidTemplateRef","description":"Integration template. MUST be registered at the maintainer; MUST declare a `kind` other than `\\"admin\\"`."},"adminTemplate":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/DidTemplateRef","description":"Optional admin-DID template. When present, the maintainer mints a fresh long-term admin DID + keys, binds the authorization VC + ACL row to it, and rolls the holder over from the ephemeral did:key in the same transaction. When absent, the authorization VC\'s subject and ACL row are bound to the ephemeral `holder`, which the operator is expected to swap via `acl/swap-key/0.1` before steady-state operation. MUST declare `kind == \\"admin\\"` when present."},"note":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":1024,"description":"Free-form operator note carried into the maintainer\'s audit log."}}},"AdminRotationAsk":{"\$anchor":"admin-rotation-ask","title":"AdminRotationAsk","description":"Admin-only mint. No integration DID is produced. Used by holders that bring (or will mint elsewhere) their own integration-side identity and only need an admin credential at this maintainer.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["type","adminTemplate"],"properties":{"type":{"const":"adminRotation"},"contextHint":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"Hint for the admin grant\'s target context. The wire `payload.context` is authoritative."},"adminTemplate":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/DidTemplateRef","description":"Admin-DID template. MUST be registered at the maintainer and MUST declare `kind == \\"admin\\"`."},"note":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":1024,"description":"Free-form operator note carried into the maintainer\'s audit log."}}},"DidTemplateRef":{"\$anchor":"did-template-ref","title":"DidTemplateRef","description":"Reference to a DID template already registered at the maintainer. Inline template definitions are deliberately not supported — templates must be uploaded out-of-band first (operator-authored or built-in) so the maintainer can validate `vars` against the template\'s declared schema.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["name"],"properties":{"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":128,"description":"Template name as registered at the maintainer (built-in or operator-uploaded). Examples of built-ins shipped with VTA deployments: `didcomm-mediator`, `vta-admin`, `did-hosting-control`, `did-hosting-daemon`, `did-hosting-server`."},"vars":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"default":{},"description":"Variable bindings the maintainer feeds to the template renderer. MUST satisfy the template\'s `requiredVars`; values for `optionalVars` MAY be supplied. Unknown vars are rejected with `provision/integration:templateVarsInvalid`."}}},"DataIntegrityProof":{"\$anchor":"data-integrity-proof","title":"DataIntegrityProof","description":"W3C Data Integrity proof. Spec body pins cryptosuite and proofPurpose; this schema permits the standard property bag so future cryptosuites can ride the same shape.","type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["type","cryptosuite","verificationMethod","proofPurpose","proofValue"],"properties":{"type":{"const":"DataIntegrityProof"},"cryptosuite":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"This version pins `eddsa-jcs-2022`. Maintainers MUST reject other values until a future minor extends the allowlist."},"verificationMethod":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"DID URL with fragment. The DID portion (left of `#`) MUST equal `holder`."},"created":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"proofPurpose":{"const":"authentication"},"proofValue":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"Multibase-encoded Ed25519 signature."}}},"Response":{"\$anchor":"response","title":"Provision Integration — response payload","description":"Carried in a Trust Task document whose type is https://trusttasks.org/spec/provision/integration/0.1#response. The sealed `bundle` is the secret-bearing artefact; `summary` is non-secret audit metadata.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["bundle","digest","summary"],"properties":{"bundle":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"OpenPGP-style ASCII-armored ciphertext of `SealedPayloadV1`. HPKE base mode, X25519-HKDF-SHA256 KEM, ChaCha20-Poly1305 AEAD, info string `vta-sealed-transfer/v1`. Recipient is the X25519 derivation of `request.holder`\'s Ed25519 pubkey."},"digest":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9a-f]{64}\$","description":"SHA-256 of the armored ciphertext, lowercase hex. Used by holders that pin the bundle out-of-band."},"summary":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/ProvisionSummary","description":"Non-secret audit metadata. MUST NOT include any private key material; the bundle is the only secret-bearing field."},"ext":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Ext"}}},"ProvisionSummary":{"\$anchor":"provision-summary","title":"ProvisionSummary","description":"Audit-grade metadata about the provisioning outcome. Mirrors the existing `vta_sdk::provision_integration::http::ProvisionSummary` Rust type but uses camelCase wire fields per Trust Task convention.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["clientDid","bundleIdHex","secretCount","outputCount"],"properties":{"clientDid":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"Ephemeral did:key the holder signed the VP with and opens the sealed bundle with. Echo of `request.holder`."},"adminDid":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"Long-term admin DID after this provisioning. Equals `clientDid` when no admin rollover occurred (TemplateBootstrap with no `adminTemplate`); equals the freshly-minted admin DID when `adminTemplate` was used or when the ask was `adminRotation`. Maintainers that pre-date admin rollover MAY omit this; consumers SHOULD default it to `clientDid` for backward compatibility."},"adminRolledOver":{"type":"boolean","default":false,"description":"True when the maintainer minted a fresh long-term admin DID and bound the authorization VC + ACL row to it (i.e. `adminDid != clientDid`)."},"integrationDid":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"DID rendered from the integration template. Absent for `adminRotation` (no integration was rendered)."},"templateName":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"Name of the integration template that was rendered. Absent for `adminRotation`."},"templateKind":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"`kind` of the integration template (e.g. `mediator`, `did-hosting-control`, `app`). Absent for `adminRotation`."},"adminTemplateName":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"Name of the admin template that was rendered. Present when an admin DID was minted (either via `TemplateBootstrap.adminTemplate` or `adminRotation`)."},"bundleIdHex":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9a-f]{32}\$","description":"VP nonce as lowercase hex (32 characters = 16 bytes). MUST equal the `Bundle-Id` armor header of `bundle`. Cross-check anchor: a holder that decodes the VP nonce can verify the bundle they opened matches the one the maintainer minted for them."},"secretCount":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"description":"Number of DIDs the sealed bundle carries private key material for. `templateBootstrap` with no adminTemplate typically yields 1 (the integration DID\'s keys). `adminRotation` yields 0 (the `admin` field is top-level, not under `secrets`)."},"outputCount":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"description":"Number of template-declared side outputs the sealed bundle carries (`did.jsonl` logs, DIDComm service advertisements, etc.). Always 0 for `adminRotation`."},"webvhServerId":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"Identifier of the registered webvh hosting server the maintainer published the integration\'s `did.jsonl` to, if any. Absent when the integration is self-hosted or when the template did not declare a webvh server var."},"contextCreated":{"type":"boolean","default":false,"description":"True when `payload.createContext` was honoured and the maintainer provisioned the target context inline. False when the context already existed (or when `createContext` was omitted / false)."}}},"Ext":{"title":"Ext","description":"Vendor-namespaced extension object per SPEC.md §4.5.1. Each immediate key MUST be a reverse-DNS namespace; structure under each namespace is opaque to the framework.","type":"object","minProperties":1,"additionalProperties":true,"propertyNames":{"pattern":"^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*(\\\\.[a-z0-9-]+)+\$"}}}}';

